From 6c53de3c3609d2b8257e5e584f72e147da9de06f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:30:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Remove ZeroMQ implementation and public notification
 interface

After the separate default-OFF build patch, remove ZeroMQ completely for
users who deliberately choose a smaller source/dependency/interface set.
Delete its publisher and RPC implementation, CMake discovery/options and
linkage, runtime arguments including previously hidden disabled-build
arguments, logging/help categories and obsolete translated help text.
Remove dependency recipes/patches, installation and CI requirements,
examples, interface docs and functional/lint plumbing. Preserve historical
release notes and incidental opaque key/fixture strings.

Add a functional regression that requires the removed RPC and six former
publisher options to fail explicitly, checks the logging category is gone,
and proves failed option parsing does not prevent subsequent clean startup.
The existing RPC help test now reflects the removed component.

This patch removes a public API; clients must migrate separately. NNG is
neither added nor required, and remains independently selectable. There is
no claimed mining or mempool performance improvement and no consensus
change. Default daemon setup does not apply this optional patch.

Requires: build: disable ZeroMQ by default without removing its implementation
Upstream base: abd433abe04f74780744b9eac06731f3690ce68a
